# SFT execution status v0.72

2026-09-10. **The no-retry coordinator and private-package wiring are implemented;
the complete tiny CPU chain passes. Gate 5 and the real 4B import are not complete.**
This is the next bounded software stage after v0.71, not a new data-policy gate.
No real weights, trainer/tokenizer payloads or datasets were opened. No network,
GPU, inference, training, instance action, dependency installation, GitHub push
or CI run was initiated. All changes remain local.

## What finished

The new `posttraining_checkpoint_import_runner_v1.py` ties the already implemented
planner, inventory verifier and CPU kernel to the new
`posttraining_checkpoint_package_v1.py`. The executable entry is **tiny synthetic
only**: it requires the explicit fixture flag, independent base-file pin and
fixed scale caps. `run_import` rejects real execution before parsing or I/O;
approval booleans cannot unlock it.

The integrated order is:

1. Validate the pinned metadata, strict limits, single-main-thread condition and
   disjoint private paths, including physical aliases.
2. Exclusively consume a fresh attempt directory; write the STARTED marker and
   exact source config. An existing or partially created attempt cannot retry.
3. Audit the complete checkpoint and original normalized tokenizer inventory.
4. Execute the actual CPU DCP-to-HF kernel with logical write reservations and
   cooperative budget callbacks.
5. Copy the three tokenizer files byte-for-byte under their original `tokenizer/`
   paths; create the private receipt and closed checksum manifest. Verify those
   with the **unchanged frozen worker checksum consumer** through bounded reads.
6. Repeat both complete input audits, compare observed identities, and return the
   result only after the provisional completion write and final deadline check.

Failed reservations are not refunded. Failure output contains only fixed stage
and error codes; partial new outputs remain consumed. A COMPLETE file alone is
not authority: its final fsync/close or a subsequent deadline check can fail, and
even FAILED may be unwritable. Success requires the returned outcome and an
independent successful parent supervisor. This exact late-failure case is tested.

Packaging uses pinned no-symlink directory descriptors, closed inventories and
at most 1 MiB content reads/writes. Read-only 0400 tokenizer sources are accepted;
private output files must be 0600. Tokenizer values are not deserialized. Package
read accounting includes the real worker consumer, including its two manifest
reads. Successful finalization content reads are
`3 * backend_bytes + 3 * tokenizer_bytes + 2 * receipt_bytes + 3 * manifest_bytes`;
source audits and native kernel reads are separate.

Review fixes include physical alias rejection, copied caller limits, strict
integer/tied-alias checks, exact safetensors names, a bounded manifest parser that
supports more than 128 rows, and descriptor cleanup on fchmod/parent-close failure.
No previous parser, dataset, rights, worker, plan or kernel file was changed.

