## What still blocks real import

Logical byte reservations and cooperative callbacks are **not** OS-enforced
native DCP/HF/mmap read, RAM, disk-write, network or blocked-syscall limits. The
parent timeout bounds the trusted tiny test process, not hostile detached child
processes. Main-thread admission is not a process/container isolation proof.
Two audits detect observed mutations; they do not make an atomic snapshot.
Packaging hashes model output but does not independently connect safetensors
bytes to the kernel's tensor digest: a trusted, quiescent kernel-to-package
handoff is still required. Receipts prove neither origin nor real-base import.

The next existing dependency is **native host/resource admission**: integrate the
native I/O and Linux RAM/write/runtime guards, bind the exact dedicated runtime
and immutable input set, then qualify that path before an explicitly bounded
real import. No suitable real execution target has been admitted; `run_import`
therefore remains closed. No GPU is needed for this remaining importer software
work. The base remains our step-76,294 / 80B-token S3-backed pretraining checkpoint;
no base selection changed.

The downstream GPU worker/profile mismatch (FSDP/4096 versus the current worker's
DDP/4095 limit), actual data relocation and CUDA/smoke requirements remain as in
v0.70. They have not been skipped or silently marked complete. Training and
production eligibility remain false.

HEAD remains `ecc545fc423650bf1089311915290523c10b3172`; tracked and staged diffs
are unchanged. This stage created only the two new modules, three test files,
the new report/structural verification and this status successor.
